<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <head>
        <title>A border on a padded text container wraps the box, not the text run</title>
        <!-- Engine bug pinned: ribbon tabs were raw text nodes; an inline
             box paints its border around the TEXT RUN, so the active tab's
             outline appeared as detached stubs. A block/flex box with a text
             child must paint the border around the padded box. -->
        <style type="text/css">
            * { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
            body { width: 800px; background: #ffffff; font-family: "Noto Sans", sans-serif; }
            .tab { display: flex; align-items: center; width: 120px; height: 40px;
                   padding: 0 18px; border: 3px solid #2a579a;
                   font-size: 18px; color: #2a579a; background: #ffffff; }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <div class="tab">HOME</div>
    </body>
</html>
